# Weights (reference/common/typography.md): page of 200 × 200 with margins of 20, page area of 160 × 160 from
# (20, 20). Lines of 12 (Size 10); with the test metrics each character measures 5 pt whatever its weight, so the
# weight does not change the layout: each text is one line of 12, 160 wide, one after the other. The image shows the
# five weights of IBM Plex Sans in the fonts folder: 300 (Light), 400, 500 (Medium), 600 (SemiBold) and 700 (Bold).
#   light:     Weight 300. y = 20.
#   normal:    without Weight: 400. y = 32.
#   medium:    Weight 500. y = 44.
#   semibold:  Weight 600. y = 56.
#   bold:      Bold: true, which is Weight 700. y = 68.
#   run:       Weight 300 with a bold run (Markup: markdown): the run has weight 700. y = 80.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 200
		Height: 200
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
	Section:
		Text: Peso 300, ligera
			Id: light
			Typography:
				Weight: 300
		Text: Peso 400, normal
			Id: normal
		Text: Peso 500, media
			Id: medium
			Typography:
				Weight: 500
		Text: Peso 600, seminegrita
			Id: semibold
			Typography:
				Weight: 600
		Text: Peso 700, negrita
			Id: bold
			Typography:
				Bold: true
		Text: Ligera con **negrita**
			Id: run
			Typography:
				Weight: 300
				Markup: markdown
